{
 "version": 1,
 "title": "Power Up",
 "category": "Effects",
 "text": "Sound: a rising 'power up' zap: the pitch sweeping up into the note, like a charging machine or a video game bonus.\n\nHow it's built: the envelope's INVERTED output (1 at the start, falling to 0) is flipped by the Attenuverter (SCALE -1) into the oscillator's FM at 3 octaves: each note starts three octaves down and sweeps up to its pitch over the ATTACK. A square wave, a Delay.\n\nPlay: short notes, anywhere.\n\nTweak: the sweep envelope's ATTACK (the length of the rise), the oscillator's FM (from how low), the delay.",
